; AI board review of the rebased language/world-model integration.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/form-neutral-language-world-model.md"
  "Independent implementation audit; do not edit any file. Read model/form-neutral-language-world-model.fk, model/tests/form-neutral-language-world-model-band.fk, cognition/core-frequency-lift-form-neutral-crossing.fk, cognition/core-frequency-lift-dictionary.fk, form/form-stdlib/world-model.fk, model/concept-world-model.fk, and form/form-stdlib/dsv4-token-recipe-swap.fk. Freshly preflight and run the new band plus the existing dictionary, crossing, world-model, and concept-world-model bands. Pressure-test: surface changes must not change semantic nodes/relations; evidence changes must change mappings; surface->anchor and anchor->mapping queries must retain provenance; anchor->recipe and recipe->anchor direction must agree; external anchors must not enter semantic rendering; a new anchor must enter the generic wm observe/persist/orient path while remaining held open against the old known set; duplicate extension must be idempotent; mismatched anchor/alignment, index overflow, unknown category, and active-envelope overflow must rest as absence. Attack the size claim: verify size is recomputed from content rather than caller supplied, variable UTF-8/provenance bytes are included, direct graph construction cannot understate them through the public constructor, and both current size and the 16 MiB ceiling are compared only to the cited 9.103 GB DS4 baseline—not to every possible LLM. Distinguish observed graph/world integration from candidate semantics, cultural review, shard activation, tokenizer IDs, generation, and performance. Return PASS AS A BOUNDED WORLD-MODEL INTEGRATION, REVISE, or BLOCK with located executable evidence. Agreement without pressure probes is not useful.")
